{%- comment -%}
  Bassface bag — replaces Dawn's main-cart-items + main-cart-footer pair for
  templates/cart.json. Boards: `w1pQjE` 1440, `Gg2md` 1024, `NDdvm` 834,
  `r4WGv` 448, `B93pNf` 390, and `h3wEI` for the empty bag.

  ONE SECTION, NOT TWO. Dawn splits the bag across two sections so the subtotal
  can be reordered or dropped in the editor, and pays for it by keeping the
  <form> in the first and the submit button in the second, then re-rendering
  both on every quantity change. The board draws one composition — title, rule,
  rows, subtotal, checkout — with no seam a merchant would want to move, and one
  section means one round trip and one thing to swap.

  WHY IT IS NOT DAWN'S SECTION RESTYLED. Same reason as bf-main-search: the
  stock page paints itself from Dawn's colour-scheme settings, so /cart stayed
  black-on-white while the header above it followed the theme switcher — visible
  in the before-shots as a white page under a cream masthead. Every colour here
  is --bf-ink on --bf-surface. Beyond the paint, <cart-items> addresses its
  markup by Dawn's own class names (.cart-item, .cart-item__name,
  #Quantity-{n}, .loading__spinner), so keeping the element would have meant
  keeping that vocabulary inside a BEM block named `cart-line`.

  NO BREADCRUMB AND NO 48px PAGE TITLE. DESIGN-STATUS is explicit that the bag
  deliberately does not use the standard page shell: the title is a full-bleed
  wordmark fitted to the content width, and there is nothing above it.

  The <form> is real and posts to /cart. bf-main-cart.js takes over both
  controls it holds, but with the script absent a customer can still edit the
  numbers and press Checkout — Shopify processes `updates[]` on that POST before
  it forwards to checkout — and Delete is a plain link to Shopify's own
  /cart/change URL. Nothing on this page needs JavaScript to work.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'bf-reveal.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'bf-cart-line.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'bf-main-cart.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'bf-reveal.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'bf-quantity.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'bf-main-cart.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- comment -%}
  data-updated-message is what the live region says once a change has gone
  through. Composed here rather than in the script because it is a translated
  string and a money-formatted total, and both belong to the server — Dawn's own
  cart live region is this same sentence. It rides on the element rather than
  inside it so that bf-main-cart.js, which swaps the contents, has to copy the
  new one across deliberately instead of inheriting a stale figure.
{%- endcomment -%}
<bf-main-cart
  class="main-cart"
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  data-error-message="{{ section.settings.error_message | escape }}"
  data-updated-message="{{ 'sections.cart.new_estimated_total' | t }}: {{ cart.total_price | money_with_currency }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The entrance, and it is the product page's, not a new one: <bf-reveal
    type="rise"> clips a wrapper and climbs its child out from under the top
    edge, on the hero's own 1400ms quart-out. It waits on the preloader handing
    over AND on reaching the viewport, so the wordmark does not play out behind
    a curtain that has not lifted yet.

    The RESTING STATE IS THE VISIBLE ONE — nothing is hidden until bf-reveal.js
    adds `is-concealed`. A blocked script leaves a plain, readable bag rather
    than a page of empty boxes.

    --reveal-index is the stagger, one step per row, so the list is dealt out
    rather than arriving as a block. The hero is 0 by default; the rows start at
    1 and the summary follows the last of them.

    bf-main-cart.js strips these wrappers out of every re-rendered section it
    swaps in. The rise is how the page ARRIVES; replaying it because someone
    pressed + would be the page arriving again, which it did not.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="main-cart__hero">
    <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise">
      <h1 class="main-cart__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
    </bf-reveal>
    <hr class="main-cart__rule">
  </div>

  {%- if cart == empty -%}
    <div class="main-cart__empty">
      <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise" style="--reveal-index: 1">
        <p class="main-cart__empty-lines">
          <span class="main-cart__empty-line">{{ section.settings.empty_line_1 }}</span>
          <span class="main-cart__empty-line">{{ section.settings.empty_line_2 }}</span>
        </p>
      </bf-reveal>

      <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise" style="--reveal-index: 2">
        <a
          class="main-cart__cta"
          href="{{ section.settings.empty_cta_url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
        >
          {%- comment -%}
            The hover is the checkout button's, whole — see the note above it in
            this file. A second arrow parked off the left edge slides in while
            the label and the trailing arrow shift right by an arrow's width.

            `1.2em` rather than the 48 this was: 1.2em of the label's 40px
            ceiling IS 48, so the board is unchanged at 1440, and below it the
            arrow now steps down with the label instead of staying 48 against
            24px type. bf-main-cart.css repeats the figure as --main-cart-cta-arrow
            — the two have to agree or the incoming arrow lands short of where
            the label left.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="main-cart__cta-icon main-cart__cta-icon--lead" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'bf-icon', icon: 'arrow-up-right', size: '1.2em' -%}
          </span>
          <span class="main-cart__cta-label">{{ section.settings.empty_cta_label }}</span>
          <span class="main-cart__cta-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'bf-icon', icon: 'arrow-up-right', size: '1.2em' -%}
          </span>
        </a>
      </bf-reveal>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <form action="{{ routes.cart_url }}" method="post" novalidate>
      <div class="main-cart__items">
        {%- for item in cart.items -%}
          <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise" style="--reveal-index: {{ forloop.index }}">
            {%- render 'bf-cart-line',
              item: item,
              index: forloop.index0,
              remove_label: section.settings.remove_label,
              type_label: section.settings.type_label
            -%}
          </bf-reveal>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      <div class="main-cart__summary">
        <div class="main-cart__totals">
          <div class="main-cart__subtotal">
            <span class="main-cart__subtotal-label">{{ section.settings.subtotal_label }}</span>
            <span class="main-cart__subtotal-value">{{ cart.total_price | money }}</span>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Cart-level discounts sit under the subtotal rather than beside it:
            the board has one row and no second column, and an order discount
            that moved the amount without saying why is the one thing on this
            page a customer would dispute.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if cart.cart_level_discount_applications.size > 0 -%}
            <ul class="main-cart__discounts" role="list">
              {%- for discount in cart.cart_level_discount_applications -%}
                <li class="main-cart__discount">
                  {{ discount.title }} (−{{ discount.total_allocated_amount | money }})
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}

          <p class="main-cart__note">{{ section.settings.tax_note }}</p>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          name="checkout" is what tells /cart to forward to the checkout after it
          has applied any `updates[]` the form carries. Same button with or
          without the script — nothing here is a JavaScript-only control.

          Two faces stacked in one grid cell, rolled through by bf-main-cart.js
          writing data-state on the button. The product page's Add to Bag has
          four because it stays on the page and has a result to report; this one
          has two because a checkout LEAVES, and the only thing to say is that
          the wait has started. Without it the button is pressed, nothing visibly
          happens for as long as Shopify takes to answer, and it gets pressed
          again.

          The hover is the product page's, whole: a second arrow parked off the
          left edge slides in while the label and the trailing arrow shift right
          by an arrow's width. `1.2em` is that width, and bf-main-cart.css
          repeats the figure as --main-cart-checkout-arrow — the two have to
          agree or the incoming arrow lands short of where the label left.

          aria-hidden on the pending face keeps the button's accessible name
          "Checkout" for anyone arriving mid-roll; the wait itself reaches
          assistive tech through aria-disabled.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button class="main-cart__checkout" type="submit" name="checkout">
          <span class="main-cart__checkout-face main-cart__checkout-face--idle">
            <span class="main-cart__checkout-arrow main-cart__checkout-arrow--lead" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- render 'bf-icon', icon: 'arrow-up-right', size: '1.2em' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="main-cart__checkout-label">{{ section.settings.checkout_label }}</span>
            <span class="main-cart__checkout-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- render 'bf-icon', icon: 'arrow-up-right', size: '1.2em' -%}
            </span>
          </span>

          {%- comment -%}
            Three real full stops, not drawn circles: they inherit the face and
            its 64px size, so they sit on the baseline as an ellipsis rather than
            as three shapes that happen to be near some text.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="main-cart__checkout-face main-cart__checkout-face--pending" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="main-cart__checkout-label">
              {{- section.settings.pending_label -}}
              <span class="main-cart__checkout-dot">.</span>
              <span class="main-cart__checkout-dot">.</span>
              <span class="main-cart__checkout-dot">.</span>
            </span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </form>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    One live region for the whole page, holding whatever the last mutation did —
    "Removed Afrojack …", "Bag updated". The per-line errors beside each row are
    role="status" in their own right; this one exists because a REMOVED line
    takes its own error node with it, so there would otherwise be nothing left
    in the document to announce the thing that just happened.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="visually-hidden" role="status" data-cart-status></p>
</bf-main-cart>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Set at a size fitted to an 8-character word. A longer heading renders smaller — see bf-main-cart.css.",
      "default": "YOUR BAG"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subtotal_label",
      "label": "Subtotal label",
      "default": "Subtotal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tax_note",
      "label": "Note under the subtotal",
      "default": "Taxes and shipping will be calculated at checkout."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "checkout_label",
      "label": "Checkout button",
      "default": "Checkout"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pending_label",
      "label": "Checkout button, while waiting",
      "info": "Shown with an animated ellipsis after it while the browser leaves for the checkout.",
      "default": "Checking out"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Line items"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "type_label",
      "label": "Product type prefix",
      "info": "Renders as \"Type: Oversized T-Shirt\".",
      "default": "Type:"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "remove_label",
      "label": "Remove link",
      "default": "Delete"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "error_message",
      "label": "Update failed message",
      "default": "That didn't go through. Try again."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Empty bag"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "empty_line_1",
      "label": "First line",
      "default": "Not even one tee?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "empty_line_2",
      "label": "Second line",
      "default": "That's sad."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "empty_cta_label",
      "label": "Link label",
      "default": "Explore the shop"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "empty_cta_url",
      "label": "Link",
      "info": "Defaults to all products."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
